@meta title="Users API" version=2 owner="platform-team"

@h1 Users API [#root]
@p Versioned REST endpoints for user identity, profile, and access tokens. All
@p responses are JSON and use UTC ISO-8601 timestamps.

@h2 Authentication [#auth]
@p All requests require a bearer token in the `Authorization` header.

@code lang=http [#auth-example]
~~~
GET /v2/users/42 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer ya29.A0AfH6...
Accept: application/json
~~~

@h2 GET /v2/users [#list-users]
@p Return a paginated list of users. Cursor-based pagination — pass the
@p `next_cursor` from the previous response to fetch the next page.

@h3 Query parameters [#list-users-params]
@ul
- `limit` (integer, 1..200, default 50)
- `cursor` (opaque string, optional)
- `q` (free-text search, optional)
- `include_archived` (boolean, default false)

@h3 Example response [#list-users-response]
@code lang=json
~~~
{
  "users": [
    {"id": 42, "email": "alice@example.com", "created_at": "2026-04-01T10:00:00Z"},
    {"id": 43, "email": "bob@example.com",   "created_at": "2026-04-02T11:30:00Z"}
  ],
  "next_cursor": "eyJsYXN0X2lkIjo0M30="
}
~~~

@h2 POST /v2/users [#create-user]
@p Create a new user. Returns 201 with the created entity.

@h3 Request body [#create-user-body]
@code lang=json
~~~
{
  "email": "carol@example.com",
  "name": "Carol Danvers",
  "roles": ["editor"]
}
~~~

@h3 Errors [#create-user-errors]
@ul
- 400 — missing or malformed field
- 409 — email already in use
- 422 — role does not exist
- 500 — internal error (retry with exponential backoff)

@h2 Rate limits [#rate-limits]
@quote source="ops-runbook"
> Default limit: 1000 req/min/token.
> 429 responses include `Retry-After` in seconds.
> Burst tolerance: 50 above the steady rate for 10 seconds.

